The loop now uses a range-based `for` with a const reference instead of indexed access. It drops the repeated `size()` call and the `(int)` cast on each iteration, which gives the compiler a simple pointer walk to optimize. The sum and the return value are unchanged.

```cpp
int MesgDefinition::GetDeveloperFieldTotalSize() const
{
	int totalSize = 0;

	for (const auto& field : devFields)
	{
		totalSize += field.GetSize();
	}

	return totalSize;
}
```